{"args":{"key":"ses_df0838e72ffeMD2Sd4Yn817mX8"},"call":"markdown","reply":{"id":19,"markdown":"# The session list jumps to the top when a session finishes. Find out why and fix …\n\n**You**\n\n> The session list jumps to the top when a session finishes. Find out why and fix it.\n\n- *Read* `src/sidebar.rs`\n\n- *Search in files* `rows.clear`\n\n- *Edit* `src/sidebar.rs`\n\n- *Bash* `./run-tests.sh`\n\nFound it. `rebuild()` in `src/sidebar.rs` clears **every row** whenever one session's status changes, so the list view loses its place and jumps to the top.\n\nThe fix keeps the rows and changes only what's different:\n\n```rust\nlet fresh = project_rows(project, input);\nmerge_by_key(&mut rows, fresh);\n```\n\nAll 112 tests pass."}}
